# Force LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# Without this, Git on Windows (core.autocrlf=true, which is the default there)
# checks text files out with CRLF. docker-compose mounts ./backend into the
# Linux backend container, so a CRLF entrypoint.sh arrives with its shebang
# reading "#!/bin/sh\r" and the container dies in a restart loop with:
#
#     exec ./entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
#
# which names the wrong thing entirely and costs an hour to diagnose. Every
# text file in this repository is either read by a Linux container or by a
# tool that is happy with LF, so LF everywhere is simply correct.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell scripts must never be CRLF, whatever a local Git config says.
*.sh text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Binary artifacts: never touch these.
*.pkl binary
*.pt binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
